Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:30:27 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 408/443] [ae-patch] Reactivate the iOS audio session before a
 Voice mode mic start

On iOS 18 WebKit sets the audio session inactive when an audio clip longer than 0.95 s ends, and webkitSpeech recognition never reactivates it, so every later take heard nothing. A long clip's end now marks the session, and the next WebKit recognizer start (the toggle path and the silent restart) first opens a throwaway microphone stream, stops its tracks and logs, capped at 1.5 s. The mic start log gains sessionState and reactivated. The keyboard button in the Voice approval row now matches the height of the text buttons beside it.
